 "_scans_note": "2026-11-03: nine volumes are on Project Gutenberg, proofread by Distributed Proofreaders from the 1914 Houghton Mifflin reissue (the 1874-1875 plates; Minor Poems from a c.1900 printing), so the Gutenberg text is now the reading of record for them. The Internet Archive scan each was first taken from is listed here as the page-image reference. Measured against the raw OCR: the same stories in the same order, and the Gutenberg text fills leaves the scans lack (Exile, Intellect, Comedy, Childhood). The OCR fix list for vol. 3 (data/ocr-fixes/vol3littleclassi00john.json) is kept as the scan's correction but no longer feeds the shelf.",
